jobs.description:
Are you ready to apply your accounting skills in a challenging role within a growing and international environment? Do you enjoy ensuring financial records are accurate, compliant, and impeccably organized? 

We are looking for a Junior Accountant to join the finance team for a company in Leuven.

Your responsibilities will include:

AP accounting

• Register incoming invoices according to Belgian accounting and VAT principles and get them through
the approval cycle;
• Payments of suppliers and reconciliation of outgoing payments;
• Review and register expense notes.
General accounting

• Book and reconcile bank statements;
• Register journal entries;
• Register payroll bookings;
• Register fixed assets and book depreciations;
• Register prepaid expenses and provisions;
• Filing Belgian VAT returns;
• Register prepaid expenses and provisions.

• Bachelor in a relevant field (Finance, Accountancy) or assimilated by experience.
• Excellent knowledge of English and good knowledge of Dutch (spoken & written).
• Great attention to detail and good with numbers and figures and an analytical acumen.
• Good understanding of Belgian accounting and financial reporting principles and practices.
• Excellent knowledge of MS Office and familiarity with relevant computer software. Experience with NetSuite and/or Salesforce is a plus.

The Junior Financial Markets role in the financial services industry in Bruxelles offers a unique opportunity to support banking and financial services operations.

Informations sur l'entreprise

Our client is a leading international organization known for its high-performance culture and commitment to excellence. This opportunity is ideal for ambitious young professionals looking to accelerate their career development.

Missions

As a Junior Financial Markets professional, you will:

• Support investment and portfolio management teams through financial analysis and market monitoring;
• Perform quantitative and qualitative analyses on financial instruments, market trends and investment opportunities;
• Produce regular reports and investment-related presentations for internal stakeholders;
• Assist in the monitoring of portfolio performance and risk indicators;
• Contribute to market research and the preparation of investment recommendations;
• Support regulatory, operational and reporting activities linked to investment management processes;
• Collaborate closely with portfolio managers, investment specialists, risk teams and other key stakeholders.

A successful Junior Financial Markets professional should have:

• Master's degree in Business Engineering/Management with option in Finance;
• An excellent level of English, as well as French or Dutch;
• Strong interest in investments, capital markets and financial products;
• Strong proficiency in Excel; familiarity with Bloomberg, Morningstar or other market data tools is an asset.
